merically when the lengths are equal — all are 3 characters so that works, but it's safer to use the text field where ES coerces to numbers).\\n\\nActually, the safest bet is: `{\\\"range\\\":{\\\"response\\\":{\\\"gte\\\":500,\\\"lte\\\":599}}}`. Range queries on a text field: ES applies the numeric comparison when the values are numeric. In the kibana sample data, response values are \\\"200\\\", \\\"301\\\", \\\"404\\\", \\\"500\\\", etc. — all numeric, so this works.\\n\\nParameters for .es-query:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"searchType\\\": \\\"esQuery\\\",\\n  \\\"esQuery\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"query\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"range\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"response\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"gte\\\\\\\":500,\\\\\\\"lte\\\\\\\":599}}}}\\\",\\n  \\\"index\\\": [\\\"kibana_sample_data_logs\\\"],\\n  \\\"timeField\\\": \\\"timestamp\\\",\\n  \\\"threshold\\\": [10],\\n  \\\"thresholdComparator\\\": \\\">\\\",\\n  \\\"timeWindowSize\\\": 5,\\n  \\\"timeWindowUnit\\\": \\\"m\\\",\\n  \\\"size\\\": 100\\n}\\n```\\n\\nthresholdComparator is \\\">\\\", threshold is [10] — fires when the count exceeds 10. This matches \\\"fire if 10 or more server errors arrive within 5 minutes.\\\"\\n\\nSchedule: every 1 minute → schedule_interval \\\"1m\\\".\\n\\nCreate it (it'll be disabled by default), then enable it.\\n\\nLet me first check whether the .es-query rule type is available. I could just create it, and if it fails, check list_rule_types. Let me just create it directly — the example in the tool description confirms that `.es-query` works with this consumer.\\n\"}, {\"type\": \"message\", \"content\": \"The dashboard is set up with two panels. Now I'll create an alert rule using a `.es-query` to detect when 10 or more server errors (500-599 responses) occur in a 5-minute window.\\n\\n\"}, {\"type\": \"tool_call\", \"name\": \"create_alert_rule\", \"arguments\": {\"name\": \"LOC-374c30a4 5xx errors\", \"rule_type_id\": \".es-query\", \"consumer\": \"stackAlerts\", \"params\": {\"searchType\": \"esQuery\", \"esQu